# Whitelist approach: ignore EVERYTHING, then allow only safe source files.
# This guarantees secrets (config.json, token.json, client_secret.json) and all
# junk (work/, logs/, .github/ stray copies, *.bat, *.ps1, etc.) are
# NEVER committed or pushed to GitHub.
*
!.gitignore
!ultimate_shorts_agent.py
!make_muli_video.py
!requirements.txt
!topic_bank.json
!slideshow_topics.json

# The runner builds the video in the cloud, so music has to travel with the
# repo -- tracks sitting only on the laptop never reach it. Each parent
# directory needs its own negation, because git will not descend into an
# excluded directory to find un-excluded files inside it.
#
# Only two sources belong here, both free of Content ID risk for the channel:
# YouTube Audio Library tracks, and beds this channel commissioned itself from
# Higgsfield's Sonilo model (assets/music/emotional/muli_theme_*.mp3).
!assets/
!assets/music/

# The cast sheet every Muli scene is drawn from. It lives on the Desktop, so a
# copy travels with the repo rather than existing only on one laptop.
!assets/cast_sheet.jpg
!assets/cast_sheet_2.jpg
!assets/cast_sheet_3.jpg
!assets/music/*/
!assets/music/*/*.mp3
!assets/music/*/*.m4a
!assets/music/*/*.wav
